    "tranche": "T4",
    "tranche_reason": "The README uses the refusal direction from Arditi et al. as the object of an interpretability analysis, but does not test whether removing or adding it changes refusal behavior.",
    "gate_note": "The README reports token-space projections, sparse reconstruction, and logit deltas for a refusal vector. These measure lexical or logit associations, not refusal rates or other behaviors named by the claim versions, so the rows are recorded under none.",
    "test_reason": "The README treats the Arditi et al. refusal direction as an object to interpret in token space. It reports vocabulary projections, sparse token reconstructions and token logit deltas under steering. It reports no refusal rates, ablation outcomes or capability checks, so no version is tested.",
    "authors_conclusion": "Correct. The README concludes that the refusal vector has a consistent lexical core (prohib, illegal, harm, forbidden, cannot). This core dominates both static projections and dynamic logit deltas.",
    "recipe": "different",
    "recipe_differences": "Tool repository accompanying an interpretability paper. It analyzes a refusal vector using vocabulary projection, sparse dictionary learning, and controlled logit comparison rather than testing the original causal ablation recipe.",
    "method_sensitivity": "The README describes logit comparisons for harmless prompts at α = +1 and harmful prompts at α = −1; no sensitivity analysis is stated.",
    "fits_no_version": [
      {
        "finding": "Vocabulary projection and sparse reconstruction of the refusal vector give refusal-related tokens top scores (harmful +10.25, prohib weight +0.0437).",
        "proposed_claim": "The refusal direction aligns with a compact set of refusal-associated token embeddings in output space.",
        "row_ids": [
          "r1",
          "r2",
          "r3",
          "r4",
          "r5",
          "r6",
          "r7",
          "r8"
        ]
      },
      {
        "finding": "Adding the vector (α=+1) on harmless prompts raises logits of prohibition tokens (prohib +7.09). Subtracting it (α=−1) on harmful prompts raises logits of affirmation tokens (great +4.40).",
        "proposed_claim": "Steering with the refusal direction shifts output logits along a prohibition versus affirmation lexical axis.",
